 "remarks": "Welcome to 7 Hamilton Avenue, Unit 22, a first-floor 2-bedroom, 1-bath apartment on a quiet residential cul-de-sac in South Norwalk. The open floor plan features hardwood floors in the living room and opens to a private balcony for outdoor space. Recent updates include updated kitchen cabinets, a new refrigerator, a new bathroom vanity, and neutral paint throughout, so it's move-in ready. In-unit laundry and two dedicated parking spots make daily life easy.  The location does a lot of the work. Walk to the South Norwalk Metro-North station, with I-95 and local bus routes just minutes away for a simple commute to Stamford or Manhattan. SoNo's restaurants and waterfront, the Maritime Aquarium, Stepping Stones Museum, and The SoNo Collection are all close by. Come home to a quiet street with everything South Norwalk offers right around the corner. Available now. Small dogs allowed.  If the landlord has a weight limit or a stance on cats, put it in the listing. \"Small\" is vague enough that you'll get calls about 60-pound labs, and a line like \"Small dogs under 25 lbs considered\" would filter those out.",
